WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.210
Here's y equals x squared minus two.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:06.570
It crosses the x-axis at
the square root of two.

3
00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.470
Start at x equals one.

4
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.590
Follow the tangent down to
the x-axis: one point five.

5
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.670
Again from there: one point
four one six six seven.

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.650
Then the screen freezes.

7
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.900
How could a machine reach ten
decimal places in just four steps?

8
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.840
In this mission, you'll use a
tangent as a stand-in for the curve:

9
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.790
where it crosses the axis
is a better estimate.

10
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.710
You'll turn that into the
Newton Raphson formula:

11
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:38.370
x n plus one equals x n minus
f of x n over f dash of x n.

12
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.210
Your mission: explain how four quick
steps can pin down the square root of two

13
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.010
to ten decimal places.
